<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Main-Neckar Railway</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1846">1846</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Main-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neckar">Neckar</a> Railway is a railway line in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> linking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt">Darmstadt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heidelberg">Heidelberg</a>, with a branch to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mannheim">Mannheim</a>. It was built jointly by the Free City of Frankfurt, the Grand Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a> and the Grand Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a> and opened in 1846. It remains one of the busiest north-south rail routes in Germany.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/main-neckar-railway.jpg" alt="Main-Neckar Railway" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Brandrodungswanderfeldhackbau · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bahntrasse.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
